  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">COVID-19: Health Expenditure and Livelihoods Support Progam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The HEALS program will support the government&apos;s response to the potentially
catastrophic health and economic impacts of the coronavirus disease (COVID-19), anchored by its $45.8 million COVID-19 Preparedness and Response Plan.2 The government is implementing a comprehensive response package that covers (i) strengthening the health system&apos;s capacity for enhanced surveillance, infection control, and potential case management; (ii) providing economic relief and recovery assistance to businesses adversely affected by the prevailing travel restrictions; and (iii) mitigating impacts on the RMI&apos;s most vulnerable communities, all within the context of a sound and sustainable fiscal framework. The RMI meets all the access criteria for the CPRO.</narrative>
  </description>
